cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its simulation results, please cite this repository."
type: software
title: "Khai Sang Thien Co: Reproducible 6/55 Lottery Simulations"
authors:
  - family-names: "Huynh"
    given-names: "Kim-Hue"
date-released: "2026-11-25"
repository-code: "https://github.com/JenllyHuynh/khai-sang-thien-co"
url: "https://github.com/JenllyHuynh/khai-sang-thien-co"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Reproducible simulations of ticket concentration, historical predictive
  overfitting, and participation under assumed near-miss responses in an
  idealized fair 6/55 lottery. Includes frozen experiment evidence, source
  snapshots, and a recent-frequency prediction baseline.
keywords:
  - lottery simulation
  - probability
  - ticket concentration
  - weighted sampling without replacement
  - overfitting
  - agent-based modeling
  - reproducibility
